Repository Structure
This repository contains the build specifications for a suite of 49 software tools for computational philosophy of science. The tools implement two methodological proposals: the STAG framework for annotating scale-dependent scientific claims, and the Null-Model Protocol for testing empirical gap claims against an explicitly specified null model.

This file explains how the repository is organised.

Top-level files
README.md — the front page of the repository. What the project is, what it does, how to get involved.

STRUCTURE.md — this file. How the repository is organised.

BUILD_SPECIFICATIONS.md — the full build specifications for all 49 apps. One file. The catalogue.

CONTRIBUTING.md — how to contribute to the project.

LICENSE — the license.

Folders
specs/ — the individual build specifications for each app, grouped by layer.

specs/01-foundation/ — the six foundation tools that everything else depends on.

specs/02-annotation-and-statistics/ — the eight tools that record and test claims.

specs/03-storage-and-audit/ — the nine tools that store and present the records.

specs/04-domain-registries/ — the twenty domain registries that apply the same pattern to different fields.

specs/05-meta-level/ — the four meta-level tools that watch over everything else.

specs/06-orchestrator-and-services/ — the orchestrator and the autofill service.

policy/ — the policy documents. Data policy, privacy policy, governance, security, sustainability.

codebook/ — the four source documents that the specifications are based on.

docs/ — longer documents. Walkthroughs, tutorials, guides.

examples/ — worked examples.

schemas/ — the JSON Schema and SHACL schema files.

The five layers
The 49 apps are organised into five layers. Each layer builds on the one below it.

Layer 1. The foundation. Six tools. These are the base. Everything else depends on them.

Layer 2. The annotation and statistical tools. Eight tools. These do the core work: record a claim, test a claim.

Layer 3. The storage, visualisation, and audit tools. Nine tools. These store and present the records.

Layer 4. The domain registries. Twenty tools. These are the same pattern applied to different fields. Each one is a registry of claims, with evidence, status, and provenance.

Layer 5. The meta-level tools. Four tools. These watch over everything else.

Plus the orchestrator and the autofill service. Two more.

How to navigate
If you want to understand the project, start with the README.md.

If you want to see the full catalogue, open BUILD_SPECIFICATIONS.md.

If you want to see the individual specifications, open the specs/ folder. Each subfolder is a layer. Each file in a subfolder is one app.

If you want to build one app, pick one from specs/01-foundation/. They are the smallest and the simplest.

If you want to understand the policies, open the policy/ folder.

If you want to understand the source material, open the codebook/ folder.

